  "notes": [
    "Hand-assembled, not generated by `tubuild.py create`: tu_map cannot segment arm9/main, so there was no candidate id to create from. The schema follows arm9/G2.",
    "Every existing linker name is kept: the eight GX:: setters keep their namespace spelling (_ZN2GX..Et, u16 parameter), and the address-named members, DisableVramBanks and Vram__Map stay under extern \"C\" because their callers name them that way. Renaming them to their SDK names is a separate change across those callers.",
    "The state block keeps its ROM name data_020a6088; its thirteen u16 fields are named after the SDK's VRAM users. The per-field data_020a608a..data_020a60a0 symbols are untouched; the wrappers reach them as fields of the block.",
    "The file is written ROM-descending because mwccarm emits .text in reverse source order; the emitted object carries the 41 functions ascending 0x02053e1c..0x02054d38."
